1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:01,854
An angle is made by two rays that start

2
00:00:01,854 --> 00:00:04,625
at the same point. The common point is the

3
00:00:04,625 --> 00:00:06,907
vertex, and the two rays are the arms of

4
00:00:06,907 --> 00:00:10,783
the angle. An angle also separates the plane into

5
00:00:10,783 --> 00:00:14,011
an interior, a boundary and an exterior.

6
00:00:14,627 --> 00:00:18,167
We see angles everywhere. Think of a door: as

7
00:00:18,167 --> 00:00:20,042
it opens, the space between the door and the

8
00:00:20,042 --> 00:00:22,127
frame grows wider. Now think of the hands of

9
00:00:22,127 --> 00:00:25,807
a clock: as they move apart, they also make

10
00:00:25,807 --> 00:00:30,067
an angle. If we keep only the two directions,

11
00:00:30,067 --> 00:00:32,178
we are left with two rays starting at one point.

12
00:00:32,793 --> 00:00:36,270
Let us build that angle. Start with a point

13
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:39,373
O, and draw one ray from it, ray OB.

14
00:00:39,373 --> 00:00:42,361
Now draw a second ray from the same point

15
00:00:42,361 --> 00:00:46,073
O: ray OA. The opening between them is the

16
00:00:46,073 --> 00:00:47,873
angle, and we write it as angle AOB. Two

17
00:00:47,873 --> 00:00:51,824
rays with a common endpoint make an angle.

18
00:00:52,507 --> 00:00:56,293
Every angle has two named parts. The common endpoint

19
00:00:56,293 --> 00:00:59,978
is the vertex, so here the vertex is O.

20
00:00:59,978 --> 00:01:02,047
The two rays are the arms: ray OA is

21
00:01:02,047 --> 00:01:04,401
one arm, and ray OB is the other. The

22
00:01:04,401 --> 00:01:08,338
arms are also called the sides of the angle.

23
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:12,360
Now the naming rule. With three letters, the vertex

24
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:16,260
must be the middle letter: angle AOB is correct.

25
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:19,680
Angle BOA is also correct, because O is still

26
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:22,513
in the middle. But angle OAB has A in

27
00:01:22,513 --> 00:01:25,100
the middle, and angle ABO has B in the

28
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:28,102
middle. Those are not names of this angle, because

29
00:01:28,102 --> 00:01:31,351
the vertex O is not in the middle.

30
00:01:31,957 --> 00:01:34,506
Notice that angle AOB and angle BOA name the

31
00:01:34,506 --> 00:01:37,907
same angle. Reading the arms in the other order

32
00:01:37,907 --> 00:01:41,180
does not change the opening. And when there is

33
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:44,063
only one angle at O, we may name it

34
00:01:44,063 --> 00:01:45,368
simply as angle O.

35
00:01:45,875 --> 00:01:49,135
An angle divides the plane around it. The region

36
00:01:49,135 --> 00:01:51,215
between the two arms is called the interior of

37
00:01:51,215 --> 00:01:54,473
the angle. A point X that lies between the

38
00:01:54,473 --> 00:01:57,435
arms is in the interior. The interior follows the

39
00:01:57,435 --> 00:02:00,546
arms outward, however far they are extended.

40
00:02:01,175 --> 00:02:03,917
What about the arms themselves? A point S on

41
00:02:03,917 --> 00:02:05,830
one of the arms lies on the angle itself;

42
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:09,418
the arms are its boundary. A point Z outside

43
00:02:09,418 --> 00:02:12,475
the opening is in the exterior. So an angle

44
00:02:12,475 --> 00:02:18,246
separates the plane into three parts: interior, boundary and exterior.

45
00:02:18,758 --> 00:02:20,526
Let us sort three points on one angle. Here

46
00:02:20,526 --> 00:02:24,318
is angle PQR, with its vertex at Q. Point

47
00:02:24,318 --> 00:02:26,976
N lies on an arm, so it is on

48
00:02:26,976 --> 00:02:31,238
the boundary. Point M is between the arms, so

49
00:02:31,238 --> 00:02:33,798
it is in the interior, and point T is

50
00:02:33,798 --> 00:02:36,049
outside, in the exterior.

51
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:40,470
Your turn. Four quick checks. First: in angle COD,

52
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:44,090
name the vertex and the two arms. Second: this

53
00:02:44,090 --> 00:02:48,600
angle has vertex Q. Give two valid three-letter names.

54
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:52,016
Third: point M, point N and point T. And

55
00:02:52,016 --> 00:02:55,421
last of all: which of these names is wrong?

56
00:03:06,323 --> 00:03:09,063
In angle COD the vertex is O, and the

57
00:03:09,063 --> 00:03:12,003
arms are OC and OD. For the second: angle

58
00:03:12,003 --> 00:03:16,443
AQB and angle BQA, because the vertex Q stays

59
00:03:16,443 --> 00:03:20,625
in the middle. And point M is in the

60
00:03:20,625 --> 00:03:24,843
interior, point N is on the boundary, and point

61
00:03:24,843 --> 00:03:28,427
T is in the exterior. The wrong name is

62
00:03:28,427 --> 00:03:32,203
angle ABO, because its middle letter is B and

63
00:03:32,203 --> 00:03:33,814
not the vertex O.

64
00:03:34,436 --> 00:03:37,412
One last look. Two rays with a common endpoint

65
00:03:37,412 --> 00:03:39,976
make an angle. That common endpoint is the vertex,

66
00:03:39,976 --> 00:03:42,599
and the two rays are the arms. When you

67
00:03:42,599 --> 00:03:45,180
name an angle with three letters, the vertex goes

68
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:48,282
in the middle. And the angle separates the plane

69
00:03:48,282 --> 00:03:53,016
into its interior, its boundary and its exterior. Build,

70
00:03:53,016 --> 00:03:58,266
name, locate. Thank you for watching, and see you

71
00:03:58,266 --> 00:03:59,347
in the next lesson.
